# Prerequisites
*.d

# Compiled Object files
*.slo
*.lo
*.o
*.obj

# Precompiled Headers
*.gch
*.pch

# Linker files
*.ilk

# Debugger Files
*.pdb

# Compiled Dynamic libraries
*.so
*.dylib
*.dll
*.so.*


# Fortran module files
*.mod
*.smod
# ...but Go's module manifest is not one of them. Without this the ring's Go
# stage has no module in a fresh clone, `go build` searches upward, finds the
# repository root instead, and the build dies at stage 3 of 6 — which reads as
# "the analyzer found nothing" rather than "four fifths of the ring never
# compiled".
!go.mod
!go.sum

